-- DICT-SEMANTICS §3 W3 (method-scheme fidelity), CONSTRAINT axis.
--
-- SPEC ANSWER (hand-derived): `mkv : a -> b` quantifies `b` at the METHOD level;
-- W3 requires the impl body to inhabit that scheme with `b` RIGID -- "the body
-- may not instantiate a `b ∈ b̄` to a constructed type". A body of `42` needs
-- `Num b`, a constraint the declared scheme does not license, so every caller's
-- free choice of `b` (a type with no `Num` impl) would break. REJECT.
--
-- OBSERVED: check/run/build all REJECT with `T-IMPL-TOO-SPECIFIC`. CONFORMANT.
--
-- This is the #814 vein (§10's last bullet): an impl body checked with FLEXIBLE
-- method-scheme variables pins a variable the caller owns -- a type crash when
-- pinned to a mismatched concrete type, silent EFFECT LAUNDERING when pinned to
-- an effect-bearing one. The effect axis is EFFECTS-SEMANTICS' to gate; this row
-- pins only that the type-axis check is live.
interface Mk a where
  mkv : a -> b

impl Mk Int where
  mkv _ = 42

main = println (mkv (1 : Int) : Int)
